    westernDetailEn: "The Parthenon (447–432 BCE) represents the high point of the Doric order, with optical refinements such as entasis and adjusted column spacing. Ionic and Corinthian orders developed alongside it. Greek stone and marble were obtained through extensive Mediterranean trade networks.",
    eastAsianDetailEn: "The introduction of wet-rice cultivation during the Yayoi period enlarged settled communities. Defensive moated settlements formed in many areas, with post-in-ground buildings and raised-floor granaries arranged within them; the Yoshinogari site in Saga is a representative example. Wet-rice farming and metal tools reached the Japanese archipelago from the continent in stages via the Korean Peninsula.",
