    westernDetailEn: "Joseph Paxton’s Crystal Palace (1851) enclosed about 70,000 square metres with an iron-and-glass system. The Eiffel Tower (1889) marked a high point of iron construction. Art Nouveau architects such as Victor Horta and Hector Guimard brought natural curves into architecture.",
    eastAsianDetailEn: "Ōura Cathedral, completed in 1864, is Japan’s oldest surviving church. The Rokumeikan, completed in 1883 to a design by Josiah Conder, was an early landmark of formal Western-style architecture. Giyōfū buildings, including Kaichi School, are distinctive interpretations of Western architecture by Japanese carpenters.",
